The data supports two independent root causes, both on HTTP calls, plus one propagation edge.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-preserve-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_wrong_status_code",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.attr_http_response_status_code AS client_code, s.attr_http_response_status_code AS seat_server_code, COUNT(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name = 'ts-preserve-service' AND c.attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND s.service_name = 'ts-seat-service' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "All 768 preserve POST calls to ts-seat-service show 502 at the caller while the seat server span reports 200."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, COUNT(*) AS n, MIN(message) AS example FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name = 'ts-preserve-service' AND level = 'SEVERE' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Preserve logs 771 SEVERE exceptions carrying the 502 Bad Gateway with the seat body 'Use a new seat number'."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH u AS (SELECT trace_id, CAST(duration AS DOUBLE) d, attr_status_code st FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name = 'POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve'), p AS (SELECT trace_id, CAST(duration AS DOUBLE) pd FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-preserve-service' AND span_name = 'POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve') SELECT u.st, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(quantile_cont(u.d/1e6, 0.5), 0) ui_p50_ms, ROUND(quantile_cont(p.pd/1e6, 0.5), 0) preserve_p50_ms, ROUND(quantile_cont((u.d - p.pd)/1e6, 0.5), 0) gap_p50_ms FROM u JOIN p USING (trace_id) GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "ui-dashboard's preserve requests take about 5-7 s longer than preserve's own server span (about 180 ms), a gap outside preserve."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code = 'Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, ROUND(quantile_cont(CAST(duration AS DOUBLE)/1e6, 0.95), 1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' AND span_name IN ('POST /api/v1/users/login', 'GET /api/v1/routeservice/routes', 'POST /api/v1/travelservice/trips/left', 'POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Only the preserve path is slow at ui-dashboard; login, routes and trips/left stay near normal latency."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-preserve-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, COUNT(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name = 'POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "36 of 55 ui-dashboard preserve requests return 500, matching preserve's failed responses after its seat call returns 502."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

